  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the goal is to establish a strong, informative baseline in the most promising region of the design space. config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, weighted) sits at the intersection of several key design choices: it tests whether combining image and RNA modalities with multiprofile transformer aggregation yields a competitive accuracy, while using relatively cheap encoders (pca_n2000 for RNA, resnet50 for image) to keep cost moderate. This single experiment simultaneously probes (a) multimodal vs. single-modality benefit, (b) multiprofile + transformer aggregation vs. simpler alternatives, and (c) a lightweight RNA encoder as a floor for later comparisons with scgpt/scvi_n200. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can exploit by upgrading encoders (ViT-L, scgpt); if it underperforms, it signals that the multiprofile/transformer axis or the multimodal combination needs rethinking. Expected relative cost: moderate (~50-60% of the most expensive configs using ViT-L + scgpt + transformer), since resnet50 and pca_n2000 are lightweight, though the transformer aggregation over multiple profiles adds some overhead."
}

